## 3. Domain Operational Artifacts

### 3.1 Experiment Tracking Templates (MLflow/Databricks)

From real Atlassian MLflow implementations:

```python
with mlflow.start_run(run_name=f"Model_{pd.Timestamp.now().strftime('%Y%m%d_%H%M')}"):
    # Log configuration parameters (flattened for MLflow compatibility)
    config_params = {
        'run_timestamp': pd.Timestamp.now().strftime('%Y%m%d_%H%M%S'),
        'total_models': len(production_models),
        'n_features': len(feature_set),
        # ... comprehensive parameter logging
    }
    mlflow.log_params(config_params)
    
    # Log evaluation metrics
    mlflow.log_metric('primary_metric', primary_value)
    mlflow.set_tag('performance_assessment', assess_performance(primary_value))
    
    # Log per-segment metrics
    for segment in segments:
        mlflow.log_metric(f'metric_{segment}', segment_value)
    # Log model artifact
    mlflow.<framework>.log_model(model, artifact_path="model")
```

**Standard experiment metadata includes:**
- Run name with timestamp
- All hyperparameters (flattened)
- Training/validation/test metrics
- Model artifacts (serialized model, environment files)
- Tags: team, use case, dataset version, performance assessment
- Input schema and feature metadata

### 3.2 Model Evaluation Framework

