# Research Report: MLE Role Organizational Integration — AI Employee Context

## Executive Summary

This report synthesizes findings from internal Atlassian documentation, industry frameworks, and AI employee strategy documents to define how an AI MLE (Machine Learning Engineer) employee integrates into an organization. The research covers KPIs, cross-functional collaboration patterns, team structures, guardrails/escalation policies, failure modes, and communication norms — all adapted for an autonomous AI agent rather than a human engineer.

---

## 1. KPIs and Success Metrics for the AI MLE Employee

### 1.1 Model Performance Metrics

Based on internal MLOps frameworks and ML Lens observability documentation:

| Metric Category | Specific KPIs | Measurement Method |
|---|---|---|
| **Model Quality** | Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank) | Offline evaluation on golden-truth datasets; online A/B testing |
| **Latency** | P50, P95, P99 inference latency; time-to-first-token for generative models | Real-time monitoring via SignalFx/ML Lens |
| **Throughput** | Queries per second (QPS), concurrent request handling | Load testing + production metrics |
| **Model Drift** | Cosine similarity between production embeddings and training data; KL divergence; KS test statistics | ML Lens drift detection; scheduled monitoring jobs |
| **Cost Efficiency** | Inference cost per request; training cost per model version; GPU utilization percentage | FinOps dashboards, ML Artifact Cost Monitoring |

**Source:** [Platformized ML Observability - ML Lens](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5362077533), [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356)

### 1.2 Operational Velocity Metrics

| Metric | Target | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Experiment Velocity** | Experiments per week per model family | Measures how quickly the MLE iterates on hypotheses |
| **Time-to-Production** | Days from experiment completion to production deployment | Reflects end-to-end pipeline efficiency |
| **Deployment Frequency** | Model deployments per sprint/quarter | Indicates CI/CD maturity and iteration speed |
| **Feature Reuse Rate** | % features consumed from centralized feature store vs. bespoke | Reflects platform leverage |
| **Retraining Cycle Time** | Time between drift detection and new model deployment | Measures closed-loop responsiveness |

### 1.3 Reliability and Incident Metrics

From internal incident management and on-call documentation:

| Metric | Target | Source |
|---|---|---|
| **Time to Detect (TTD)** | < 15 minutes | PIR action guidelines |
| **Time to Resolve (TTR)** | < 2 hours | PIR action guidelines |
| **Production Incident Rate** | ML-attributed incidents per quarter | HOT incident tracking |
| **Rollback Success Rate** | % successful automated rollbacks | Deployment store metrics |
| **SLO Compliance** | % time within latency/error-rate budgets | SLO control plane |

**Source:** [PIR-21119](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/inckb/pages/4203708841), [H2 Action Plan: Incident management](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/6496031494)

### 1.4 AI-Employee-Specific KPIs

From the AI Employee Strategy and Symphony documentation:

| Metric | Description |
|---|---|
| **Time-to-Delegation** | How quickly a team trusts the AI MLE to handle a complex task autonomously — the north star metric |
| **Workflows/Week Executed Autonomously** | Number of distinct MLE workflows completed without human intervention |
| **Escalation Rate** | % of tasks requiring human approval (🟡) or full escalation (🔴) |
| **Context Enrichment Rate** | How much the ORBIT context layer grows per completed work item |
| **Policy Compliance Rate** | % of actions within defined policy boundaries |

**Source:** [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831), [AIF (PAI) L3-O1-KR1: AI Employee](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/aifun/pages/6978208776)

