## 3. Guardrails and Escalation Policies

### 3.1 The3-Tier Autonomy Model

From the Atlassian Symphony AI Employee Orchestration Platform:

| Tier | Signal | Meaning | MLE Examples |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1— Autonomous** | 🟢 | Agent acts without human approval. Known pattern, within policy scope, bounded blast radius. | Routine retraining on schedule; drift monitoring; experiment logging; feature store queries |
| **2 — Confirm** | 🟡 | Agent proposes action with reasoning. Human approves with single click. | Novel model architecture deployment; cost-increasing infrastructure changes; A/B test launch |
| **3 — Escalate** | 🔴 | Agent hits a hard policy boundary. Pages human with full context and reasoning trace. | Safety threshold breach; bias/fairness check failure; cross-tenant data access; production incident |

**Critical principle**: "Policies are version-controlled, auditable, and human-authored. The AI employee proposes policy updates when it identifies gaps — humans approve all changes. Symphony's autonomy is bounded by what humans have explicitly permitted; it never exceeds it."

**Source:** [Atlassian Symphony: AI Employee Orchestration Platform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6933824809)

### 3.2 Model Safety Guardrails

From AI Risk Management and ML-Engine documentation:

| Guardrail | Threshold/Trigger | Action |
|---|---|---|
| **Model performance degradation** | Accuracy drops > X% below SLO threshold | Automated rollback to last known good model |
| **Inference latency breach** | P95 latency > defined SLO | Circuit breaker opens; traffic routed to fallback model |
| **Error rate threshold** | ≥ 20% failure rate in60-second sliding window | Circuit breaker activates (ML-Engine pattern) |
| **Data drift detection** | KS test / cosine similarity below threshold | Alert MLE; trigger retraining pipeline evaluation |
| **Bias/fairness violation** | Demographic parity / equalized odds below threshold | Block deployment; escalate to Responsible AI team |
| **Cost overrun** | Training job exceeds compute budget limit | Job terminated; escalation to resource owner |
| **Toxicity/safety filter** | Model output triggers safety classifier | Response blocked; logged for review |

**Source:** [ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6058351626), [AI Risk Management Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/aats/pages/6728253551), [AIFC Launch Risk Assessment](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/aats/pages/6439210505)

### 3.3 Deployment Guardrails

From the Policy for AI Agents in SDLC:

**Every autonomous model deployment must include:**
1. Clear intent + non-goals
2. Impacted services and files
3. Declared invariants (what must remain true)
4. Risk classification
5. Test and verification plan
6. Rollback plan
7. Post-deploy monitoring plan

**What the AI MLE must NOT do autonomously:**
- Deploy changes that widen customer data access or cross tenant boundaries
- Change authentication, authorization, billing, or compliance-sensitive logic
- Run destructive schema or data operations without expand-contract patterns
- Skip logging, monitoring, alerting, or rollback requirements
- Exceed allowed blast radius for current autonomy tier
- Proceed based on unverifiable assumptions about business intent

**Source:** [Policy for AI Agents in SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~cknott/pages/6676494313)

### 3.4 Operational Guardrails Specific to ML

From AI Risk Management Checklist:

- **Feature flags** for all ML experiences with environment-scoped rollout and instant disable
- **Observability**: trace prompts/latency, safety filter hits, cost per request, and user outcomes
- **Human-in-the-loop** escalation path for safety or policy-ambiguous cases
- **Offline and online evals** with regression gates before promotion to production
- **Review cadence**: Weekly risk triage; per-release safety/quality gate sign-off + rollback rehearsal; quarterly audit of metrics, incidents, and policy updates

### 3.5 Compute and Cost Guardrails

From Model Deployment Agility:

| Control | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **GPU budget enforcement** | Verify budget and utilization before allocation changes |
| **Auto-approval threshold** | If change is small and low-risk → auto-approve |
| **Large delta escalation** | Creates capacity review ticket with all context for human decision |
| **Autoscaling cutoff** | Alerts when load exceeds expected envelope so teams can react |
| **Load testing requirement** | Automated load testing estimates GPU needs before production |

