## 2. Cross-Functional Collaboration Patterns

### 2.1 MLE × Data Engineers

Based on the "Data Engineering for AI/ML" collaboration framework:

**Collaboration Surface:**
- **Data pipelines**: DE buildsArgo Workflows to automate ingestion and transformation; MLE consumes as training data
- **Feature Store**: DE builds centralized feature store (Tecton/MLFS); MLE discovers, reuses, and shares engineered features
- **Data Quality**: Shared ownership — DE ensures pipeline reliability, MLE validates feature distributions and schema compatibility
- **Feedback loops**: Joint troubleshooting when model performance degrades due to data issues; rapid feature ideation cycles

**Interaction Pattern for AI MLE:**
- 🟢 **Autonomous**: Consume existing features from feature store; trigger pre-approved data refresh jobs
- 🟡 **Confirm**: Request new feature pipelines; propose schema changes to existing features
- 🔴 **Escalate**: Data quality issues affecting multiple downstream consumers; privacy/compliance data access requests

**Source:** [Data Engineering for AI/ML](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203162262de7da4028af1305f51fca9685/pages/5952179286)

### 2.2 MLE × Product Managers

**Collaboration Surface:**
- **Problem Formulation**: PM defines business objectives; MLE formulates ML problems end-to-end and identifies feasibility/usability validation techniques
- **A/B Testing**: MLE designs experiments; PM defines success metrics tied to business KPIs
- **Requirements Translation**: PM communicates non-technical stakeholder needs; MLE translates to model requirements
- **Result Communication**: MLE communicates results to non-technical stakeholders through compelling data stories

**Interaction Pattern for AI MLE:**
- 🟢 **Autonomous**: Run pre-approved A/B experiments within defined guardrails; generate experiment reports
- 🟡 **Confirm**: Propose new model architectures with cost/latency tradeoffs; recommend feature prioritization changes
- 🔴 **Escalate**: Model outputs show unexpected bias; business KPI regression detected; new model use case outside approved scope

**Source:** [Machine Learning Engineer - P4 - JD](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/1372671173), [P50 Senior Machine Learning Engineer](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~455370031/pages/4166070872)

### 2.3 MLE × SREs (Site Reliability Engineers)

**Collaboration Surface:**
- **Deployment reliability**: SRE manages serving infrastructure health; MLE owns model-specific operational quality
- **Incident response**: Shared on-call for ML-specific incidents; SRE handles infrastructure, MLE handles model logic
- **Monitoring**: Joint responsibility for operational metrics (latency, error rates) + ML metrics (drift, quality)
- **Capacity planning**: MLE estimates GPU/compute needs; SRE provisions and manages autoscaling

**Interaction Pattern for AI MLE:**
- 🟢 **Autonomous**: Monitor model drift; trigger pre-approved retraining; execute automated rollback when thresholds breach
- 🟡 **Confirm**: Scale-up requests exceeding team quota; deploying new model architecture to production
- 🔴 **Escalate**: Production incident affecting customers; infrastructure failure blocking model serving; cross-tenant impact

**Source:** [Model Deployment Agility - Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CentAI/pages/6081033354), [Agentic Operations in the New SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6885869718)

### 2.4 MLE × Platform Engineers (ML Platform)

**Collaboration Surface:**
- **ML Studio**: Training orchestration, workflow scheduling, experiment tracking
- **TEAMServe**: Model serving infrastructure, deployment pipelines, canary/shadow strategies
- **ML Registry (Tarot)**: Model versioning, lineage tracking, compliance metadata
- **ML Lens**: Observability, drift alerting, performance monitoring

**Interaction Pattern for AI MLE:**
- 🟢 **Autonomous**: Use existing ML Studio workflows; register models in Tarot; configure ML Lens alerts
- 🟡 **Confirm**: Request new compute allocation; propose changes to deployment manifests; onboard new serving endpoint
- 🔴 **Escalate**: Platform outage blocking training/serving; capacity exhaustion; compliance breach detected

**Source:** [AI Platform — Team Configuration](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121a92c3ba4604d4396ab3a6ee3e5e82c60/pages/6671558667), [ML Studio Lab and Nexus](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4790486547)

### 2.5 MLE × Research Scientists

**Collaboration Surface:**
- **Paper-to-production**: Research proposes novel architectures; MLE evaluates feasibility, builds production-grade implementations
- **Experiment design**: Joint experimentation with research providing theoretical grounding, MLE providing engineering rigor
- **Model evaluation**: Research defines evaluation methodology; MLE implements evaluation pipelines

**Interaction Pattern for AI MLE:**
- 🟢 **Autonomous**: Implement approved research findings into production pipelines
- 🟡 **Confirm**: Propose architectural modifications to research recommendations for production constraints
- 🔴 **Escalate**: Research approach requires resources beyond budget; novel safety concerns with proposed model

