## 6. Communication Norms and Protocols

### 6.1 Experiment Result Sharing

| Cadence | Content | Audience | Format |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Per-experiment** | Metrics, methodology, conclusions | Team (Slack/Confluence) | Structured experiment report |
| **Weekly** | Experiment velocity, key results, blockers | Manager + stakeholders | Status update (automated by AI MLE) |
| **Quarterly** | Impact summary, roadmap progress | Leadership | Business impact narrative |

### 6.2 Model Review Process

From internal MLOps frameworks:

1. **Pre-deployment checklist** (automated by AI MLE):
   - Offline metrics pass threshold (accuracy, precision, recall)
   - Data validation tests pass (schema, ranges, missing values)
   - Performance/load tests pass (latency, throughput)
   - Bias/fairness checks clear
   - Cost estimate within budget
2. **Model review gate** (🟡 tier — requires human confirmation):
   - Human reviews evaluation report
   - Approves deployment with single click
   - OR requests additional testing/changes

3. **Post-deployment verification** (automated by AI MLE):
   - Canary metrics tracked
   - A/B comparison with statistical significance
   - Auto-rollback if metrics degrade

### 6.3 Incident Communication Protocols

From PIR documentation and incident management standards:

**During ML Incidents:**
- Immediate acknowledgment in team Slack channel
- Status updates every 30 minutes (per SLO)
- Clear severity classification with documented reasoning for changes
- Centralized communication (avoid split-brain across channels)

**Post-Incident:**
- PIR within 5 business days covering:
  1. Deployment and testing gaps
  2. TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC analysis (targets: TTD < 15 min, TTR < 2 hours)
  3. Recovery and restoration actions
  4. Monitoring and alerting improvements
  5. Prevention strategies
  6. Playbook updates
  7. Incident management process improvements

**AI MLE Difference:** The AI employee generates PIR drafts automatically from reasoning traces captured during incident response, providing full timeline and action documentation without manual effort.

**Source:** [PIR-24797](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/inckb/pages/5167990917), [HOT-143980: LLM Generated PIR](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GSRE/pages/6070021856)

### 6.4 Documentation Standards

From the "Level Up your ML Craft" guide and operational documentation:

**Required Documentation for AI MLE:**
- **Model cards**: Architecture, training data, performance characteristics, limitations, fairness analysis
- **Experiment logs**: Full metadata for reproducibility (hyperparameters, data version, code version, results)
- **Runbooks**: Step-by-step procedures for each failure mode (auto-generated and continuously updated by AI MLE)
- **Decision logs**: Rationale for model choices, architecture decisions, trade-offs evaluated
- **Deployment manifests**: Intent, scope, invariants, rollback plan, monitoring plan

**AI MLE Advantage:** "The agent summarizes every execution, accumulating local knowledge so it never solves the same problem twice. This is the operational complement to the Permanent Remediation PR — the agent improves its own model of your system alongside updating the Spec."

**Source:** [Agentic Operations in the New SDLC](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6885869718), [Level Up your ML Craft](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020b9c471b742f3414899397c898d2dd049/pages/5585955478)

### 6.5 Stakeholder Update Formats

| Stakeholder | Frequency | Content | Channel |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Engineering Team** | Daily standup | Current task, blockers, experiment results | Slack/automated digest |
| **Product Manager** | Weekly | Business metric impact, experiment pipeline status | Confluence + meeting |
| **Leadership** | Monthly/Quarterly | ROI, model portfolio health, strategic recommendations | Formal report |
| **On-call handoff** | Per rotation | Outstanding issues, watch items, in-flight work | Structured handoff doc |

