## 7. Key Differences: AI MLE Employee vs. Human MLE

| Dimension | Human MLE | AI MLE Employee |
|---|---|---|
| **Availability** | Business hours + on-call rotation | 24/7 continuous monitoring and response |
| **Context switching** | Expensive; limits WIP | Near-zero cost; can manage multiple parallel tasks |
| **Knowledge retention** | Dependent on documentation discipline | Self-evolving memory; every execution enriches context |
| **Escalation** | Self-directed judgment | Policy-bounded with explicit tier system (🟢/🟡/🔴) |
| **Creativity/ambiguity** | Excels at novel problem formulation | Requires human guidance for truly novel approaches |
| **Accountability** | Individual accountability | "The organization, not the agent, is accountable for outcomes" |
| **Trust building** | Immediate (human judgment) | Progressive: earns autonomy over time via Time-to-Delegation |
| **Failure mode** | Burnout, context loss, knowledge silos | Logic drift, policy gaps, over-confident actions |
| **Onboarding** | Weeks-months | ORBIT bootstrap (minutes-hours for context, weeks for trust) |
| **Governance** | Code review, peer review, manager oversight | Policy gates + review checkpoints + budget controls + audit trails |

